---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrafficWorkbench from '../components/TrafficWorkbench.astro';
const description = 'Analyze Nginx, Apache, and JSON access logs in your browser. Find top IPs, cloud providers, request bursts, HTTP errors, and popular paths. Share and export reports.';
---
<Layout title="Nginx & Apache Access Log Analyzer" description={description} keywords="access log analyzer, nginx log analyzer, apache log analyzer, web server logs, analyze bot traffic, IP log analysis, JSON access logs" toolId="access-log-analyzer" breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Network Tools', href: '/network-tools' }, { name: 'Access Log Analyzer' }]} jsonLd={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'SoftwareApplication', name: 'Bug Days Access Log Analyzer', applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any modern browser', description, url: 'https://bugdays.com/access-log-analyzer/', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' } }]}>
  <TrafficWorkbench mode="log" />
  <section class="traffic-guide">
    <div><h2>Read the pattern behind the requests</h2><p>Open Nginx or Apache common/combined access logs, or JSON logs with one request per line. See top client IPs, requested paths, response status counts, and a UTC request timeline. JSON logs with request durations also show median and 95th-percentile latency.</p></div>
    <div><h2>Connect requests to cloud and hosting networks</h2><p>Match logged client IPs to the same cloud, VPS, CDN, service, and crawler datasets used by our <a href="/ip-lookup/">bulk hosting IP lookup</a>. Review provider traffic alongside request volume and errors, or follow the guide to <a href="/guides/identify-cloud-hosting-ips-in-access-logs/">identifying hosting IPs in access logs</a>.</p></div>
    <div><h2>A report you can hand over</h2><p>Raw logs are processed locally; only unique IP addresses are sent for provider matching. Report links include IP evidence, path counts, and summary findings, with query strings and raw lines excluded. Export JSON to reopen later, or use CSV, Excel, and print-to-PDF.</p></div>
  </section>
</Layout>
